<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  VehicleBeastSound_Fix.xml                 Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-21
  ============================================================================

  The DogSled now pulls TWO EOPIES, and it still yelped like a dog when shot.

  Alpha Vehicles Neolithic gives the sled the flesh type `AV_WoodenAndDogVehicle`,
  whose three impact sounds all point at SoundDef `AV_BulletImpact_Wood_And_Dogs`
  (FleshTypeVehicle.xml:70-72). That SoundDef's single grain is an
  AudioGrain_SeveralFolders reading:

      Impact/Bullet_Wood  +  Pawn/Animal/Dog/Dog_Injured

  ⇒ replace the dog folder with a herbivore one. Only the DogSled uses that flesh
  type, so this is one SoundDef and it affects nothing else in the mod.

  🔴 WHY Muffalo_Pain AND NOT A GUESS. Vanilla ships its sounds inside Unity asset
  bundles - there are ZERO loose .ogg files under the game's Data folder, measured
  2026-08-21 - so no folder path can be confirmed to exist by looking at the disk,
  and a wrong clip path is a SILENT no-sound. The path below is not chosen, it is
  BORROWED: `AV_BulletImpact_Wood_And_Ox`, in this same donor mod, already reads
      Impact/Bullet_Wood  +  Pawn/Animal/Muffalo/Muffalo_Pain
  for its ox cart. A path another shipped SoundDef already resolves is a path that
  resolves. Found by indexing every clipFolderPaths in all 3,345 SoundDefs of the
  2026-08-21 dump; only three animal-injury folders are referenced anywhere in the
  build - Dog_Injured, Horse/Pain and Muffalo/Muffalo_Pain.

  Muffalo over Horse because an eopie is a large shaggy browsing herbivore rather
  than an equine, and because Muffalo is what the donor already uses for its own
  draught team - so the sled now matches the ox cart it drives beside.

  ⚠️ The whole `clipFolderPaths` list is replaced rather than the one `<li>` inside
  it. A predicate that selects an `<li>` BY ITS OWN TEXT is `li[.="..."]`, which
  RimWorld accepts and the offline validator cannot evaluate - it has no child to
  predicate on - so it would report 0 matches and look exactly like a dead xpath.
  Replacing the parent keeps both engines in agreement. Same reasoning as
  GrimTerraTexPaths_Fix.xml.

  ⛔ DO NOT EDIT THE WORKSHOP FOLDER. Steam overwrites it on the next update.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Alpha Vehicles - Neolithic</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/SoundDef[defName="AV_BulletImpact_Wood_And_Dogs"]/subSounds/li/grains/li/clipFolderPaths</xpath>
      <value>
        <clipFolderPaths>
          <li>Impact/Bullet_Wood</li>
          <li>Pawn/Animal/Muffalo/Muffalo_Pain</li>
        </clipFolderPaths>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
